irccf:MITRE_M0801 a irccf:MITREMitigation ;
    rdfs:label "Access Management" ;
    dcterms:description "Access Management technologies can be used to enforce authorization polices and decisions, especially when existing field devices do not provide sufficient capabilities to support user identification and authentication. (Citation: McCarthy, J et al. July 2018) These technologies typically utilize an in-line network device or gateway system to prevent access to unauthenticated users, while also integrating with an authentication service to first verify user credentials. (Citation: Centre for the Protection of National Infrastructure November 2010)" ;
    dcterms:source <https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0801/> ;
